{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And their corpses — it shall rise in their guilt.</b> There [in that verse], and behold, it is in the absolute state, in fire [or: as guilt-offering], on the pattern of קדש." "<b>נמסו.</b> Doubled-root verbs of the nif'al binyan."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The lemma and analysis are textually difficult. 'באשם' may mean 'in their guilt' or refer to an אשם (guilt-offering); 'באש' (in fire) is then cited separately as an example of a word appearing in the absolute state like קדש. The relationship between these terms in Ibn Ezra's Hebrew is obscure and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:36.762150592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}